\par \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} Overview}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Overview}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Overview}}{\plain \b\f6  Overview
\par }{\f6 
\par The object of the game is to get five pieces in a row before the opponent does. 
\par In this version the size of the board is 62x62 grid of squares.
\par 
\par 
\par  \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} PlayingTheGame}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Playing The Game}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} PlayingTheGame}}{\plain \b\f6 
 Playing the Game
\par }{\f6 
\par The object of the game is to be get five pieces in a row, horizontally, vertically, or diagonally, before the opponent.
\par 
\par To choose a }{\f6\uldb\cf6 Skill level}{\v\f6\cf6 SkillMenuCommands}{\f6 :
\par From the Skill menu choose Beginner, Novice, Expert or Master.
\par 
\par To Start a New Game:
\par From the Game menu Choose New, or press F2.
\par 
\par To occupy a Square:
\par Move the pointer using mouse or keyboard direction keys.
\par When the pointer is on the square you want, click the left mouse button or press ENTER.
\par \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} RulesOfTheGame}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Rules Of The Game}}{\fs16 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Rules Of TheGame}}{\plain 
\b\f6  Rules of the Game
\par }{\f6\uldb 
\par }{\f6 Noughts and Crosses rules:
\par 
\par The game board is 62x62 grid of squares.
\par 
\par To win, you must line up five pieces in a row horizontally, vertically, or diagonally.
\par \tab 
\par Players alternate taking turns until either one player wins, or no free squares remain. If neither player wins, the game is a draw.
\par 
\par \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} StrategyAndHints}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Strategy and Hints}}{\fs16 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Strategy and Hints}}{\plain 
\b\f6  Strategy and Hints
\par }{\f6\uldb 
\par }{\f6 You must try to create a situation, where you can force a win no matter the computer does.
\par 
\par The most usual winning positions are:
\par 
\par -Row of four with both ends open.  
\par -Two rows of three crossing so you can simultaniously create two rows of four.
\par -Two rows of two with both ends open crossing, so you can simultaniously create two rows of three with both ends open. 
\par -many, many other combinations.
\par 
\par The attacking player controls the game.
\par 
\par 
\par \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} GameMenuCommands}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Game Menu Commands}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Game Menu Commands}K{\footnote 
\pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Start a New Game}}{\plain \b\f6   Game Menu Commands
\par }{\f6 
\par NEW starts a new game. 
\par 
\par STATISTICS shows your wins and losses and percentage of wins. 
\par Statistics are reset every time you exit the game or change skill level. 
\par 
\par EXIT ends your Noughts and Crosses session. 
\par 
\par 
\par \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} SkillMenuCommands}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Skill Menu Commands}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Skill Menu Commands}}{\plain 
\b\f6  Skill Menu Commands
\par }{\f6 
\par Skill commands set the skill level at which the computer plays the game.
\par 
\par Beginner\tab Lowest skill level
\par Novice    \tab 
\par Expert     \tab 
\par Master    \tab Highest skill level
\par 
\par The higher the skill level is, the more time the program spends thinking its moves.
\par 
\par 
\par \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} ViewMenuCommands}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} View Menu Commands}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} View Menu Commands}}{\plain \b\f6 
 View Menu Commands
\par }{\f6 
\par ZOOM IN
\par \tab Makes the board and pieces on it look bigger
\par 
\par ZOOM OUT
\par \tab Makes the board and pieces on it look smaller
\par 
\par CENTER.
\par \tab Centerizes the display
\par 
\par COMPUTERS LAST
\par \tab Flashes the computers most recent piece on the board
\par 
\par 
\par \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} OptionsMenuCommands}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Options Menu Commands}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Options Menu Commands}}
{\plain \b\f6  Options Menu Commands
\par }\pard \li1134 {\f6 
\par }\pard {\f6 
\par USERS PIECE
\par 
\par Chooses wheather the Users piece is nought or cross.
\par 
\par 
\par WHO STARTS THE GAME
\par 
\par USER \tab \tab User starts always
\par COMPUTER \tab Computer starts always
\par ALTERNATING\tab Games are started alternating.
\par RANDOM\tab Games are started random.
\par 
\par 
\par BACKGROUND PROCESSING
\par 
\par If this option is enabled:
\par While you are thinking your move, the computer spends the time preparing responces to your possible moves. The computer doesn't always get a responce ready, so then it must continue processing after you have made your move.
\par 
\par If this option is disabled:
\par The program is idle when you are thinking your move, and starts processing only after you have placed your piece.
\par 
\par The computer makes the same move wheather BackgrounProcessing-option is enabled or not. The only difference is that you see the computers move faster if this option is enabled. 
\par 
\par If you are running some other program on the same computer, you might want to turn this option off to give more processor-time to the other program. 
\par 
\par 
\par \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} CheatMenuCommands}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Cheat Menu Commands}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Cheat Menu Commands}}{\plain 
\b\f6  Cheat Menu Commands
\par }{\f6 
\par 
\par UNDO
\par You can take away your last piece from the board.
\par This option is not available after the game has ended.
\par \tab 
\par HINT
\par If you don't have a clue where to put your piece you can ask for advise.
\par This option is not always available because there are a couple of internal states of the program where I consider it is too much work to make this hint option work. If you don't like this you can turn off BackgroundProcessing to avoid these situations. 

\par 
\par \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} InitializationFile}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Initialization File}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Initialization File}}{\plain 
\b\f6  Initialization File
\par }\pard \li1134 {\f6 
\par }\pard {\f6 
\par If you don't like the colours of the game you can change them by writing new colour values to the Initalization File 0X.INI found in your Windows directory
\par 
\par For example:
\par If you want to change the board to be green, crosses white and noughts black, write following lines to the Initialization file
\par 
\par CrossR=255
\par CrossG=255
\par CrossB=255
\par NoughtR=0
\par NoughtG=0
\par NoughtB=0
\par BoardR=0
\par BoardG=255
\par BoardB=0
\par 
\par R,G and B values stand for Red,Green and Blue intensity. The value can be any number between 0 and 255.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par \page \page }{\plain \b\f6 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 #} Keyboard}}{\fs16\up6 ${\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 $} Keyboard}}{\plain \b\f6  }{\fs16 K{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Keyboard}}{\fs16\up6 K
{\footnote \pard\plain \s245 \fs20 {\fs16\up6 K} Start a New Game}}{\plain \b\f6  Keyboard
\par }{\plain \f6 
\par }{\b\f6\ul Key\tab \tab \tab \tab Function
\par }{\f6 
\par Direction Keys\tab \tab \tab Move the pointer
\par Enter\tab \tab \tab \tab Place your piece
\par F1\tab \tab \tab \tab Open the Help Index
\par F2 \tab \tab \tab \tab Start a new game
\par ESC\tab \tab \tab \tab Minimize the Game to an icon.
\par 
\par Ctrl+I\tab \tab \tab \tab Zoom In
\par Ctrl+O\tab \tab \tab \tab Zoom Out
